  "question": {
    "text": "The major product formed when 1, 1, 1- trichloropropane is treated with aqueous potassium hydroxide is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "i8YhB",
      "text": "2 - Propanol",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9DvDt",
      "text": "Propyne",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RNBdf",
      "text": "Propionic acid",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6JgON",
      "text": "1 - Propanol",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The major product formed when 1, 1, 1-trichloro-propane is treated with aqueous potassium hydroxide is propionic acid.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Alc. KOH causes elimination in the molecule of haloalkane generally, while aq. KOH leads to substitution. Here&nbsp;aqueous&nbsp;KOH is used, substitution reaction is most preferable.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The initial reaction is the nucleophilic substitution, which will form a trihydroxy compound, since, three hydroxy&nbsp;group on one carbon is unstable and result in dehydration and form carboxylic acid.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0026260_AnsExp_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 486px; height: 113px;\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0026260_AnsExp_2.jpg\" style=\"width: 494px; height: 145px;\" /></strong></u></p></blockquote>",
